<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Bornhöved</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1227</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Bornhöved was fought on 22 July 1227 in Holstein, where an alliance of north German princes, including Count Adolf IV of Holstein, Count Henry of Schwerin, the Archbishop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bremen">Bremen</a> and the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lubeck">Lübeck</a>, defeated King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valdemar-ii-of-denmark">Valdemar II of Denmark</a>. The victory ended Danish dominance over the southern Baltic coast and restored Holstein to its counts.</p></div>
